# What the pins in sources.lock are for: build/pins-table.sh joins this file
# with sources.lock into the overview tables of the README and the release
# notes. Versions and commits come from sources.lock only, never from here.
#
#   product <id> | <name> | <sources> | <how it is tested>
#   change  <source> | <base> | <what it changes or fixes> | <how the change is tested> | <upstream>
#
# A "change" line is for every pin that is not a plain upstream release: a
# fork commit or a development commit. Fields are Markdown, one line each.
# <upstream>: the pull requests and issues (owner/repo#N, space-separated)
# that carry the change upstream; check-upstream.sh reports their state, and
# once all are merged or fixed the pin can go back to an upstream release.

product linux        | Linux client `sdl-freerdp` + `freerdp-tk` | freerdp sdl3 sdl3_ttf freetype openssl opus dav1d zlib jansson freerdp_tk python_linux_x86_64 python_linux_aarch64 | `build/check-portable.sh` (only glibc ≥ 2.34, libgcc_s and libpulse from the host), `test/smoke.sh` (starts and finds its libraries on Alma 9, Rocky 10, Debian 12/13, Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Fedora 43, Tumbleweed, Arch; there the bundled Python loads Tk and freerdp-tk)
product windows      | Windows client `sdl-freerdp.exe` + `freerdp-tk` | freerdp sdl3 sdl3_ttf freetype libressl opus dav1d zlib jansson llvm_mingw freerdp_tk python_windows_x86_64 python_windows_aarch64 | `build/check-windows.sh` (needs only Windows' own DLLs)
product macos        | macOS client `sdl-freerdp` + `freerdp-tk` | freerdp sdl3 sdl3_ttf freetype openssl opus dav1d zlib jansson freerdp_tk python_macos_arm64 python_macos_x86_64 | `build/check-macos.sh` (only macOS's own libraries and frameworks, minimum macOS 12.0, an ad-hoc signature); the bundled Python loads Tk and freerdp-tk; arm64 on macos-15, x86_64 on macos-15-intel
product windows_host | Windows host `freerdp-shadow-service` + `freerdp-shadow-cli` | freerdp_host libressl opus dav1d aom zlib jansson llvm_mingw | `build/check-windows.sh`, then `test/windows-host.ps1` on a Windows Server 2025 runner: the service runs the server as SYSTEM on the console session, Windows-account logins, AV1, Ctrl+Alt+Del and the lock screen followed, a Unix socket; and the web client logs in through websockify
product web          | Web client + freerdp-web page | freerdp sdl3_wasm sdl3_ttf freetype libressl opus dav1d zlib jansson freerdp_web | `test/wasm-session.sh`: a browser logs in to xrdp through SSH + websockify, the page served without COOP/COEP headers (as GitHub Pages)
product xrdp         | xrdp packages (.deb, .rpm) | xrdp librfxcodec libpainter xorgxrdp x264 opus pipewire_xrdp mutter | `check-deps.sh`, then `test/xrdp-session.sh`: install in a fresh container of each release, log in over RDP: an Xorg session (xorgxrdp) with an xterm, then a Wayland one (sway, unless the release is marked no-sway) captured at the client's size; the login screen lists GNOME, and KDE unless no-kde; the default is GNOME on Fedora (Wayland first), Xorg elsewhere

change freerdp          | FreeRDP master @ 670e10b29 (2026-10-28) | our release, picked from integration-latest on the fork; every client, native and web, builds it, not an upstream release; master has the Opus microphone fix #13810 that 3.32.2 lacks, upstream's hardening of 2026-10-28 (invalid order bounds, messages and fastpath input before activation, the brush cache, H.264 reset bounds, smartcard strings), and our merged AV1 #13731, sound #13732, H.264 through WebCodecs #13812, #13838, #13839, the Web Audio microphone #13811, no connection dialog window #13860, SDL3 clipboard events with every field set #13872 and hotkeys from the key event's own modifiers #13852. 4 commits of open pull requests for Emscripten builds (not compiled natively): clipboard #13733 (as of 2026-10-25), the MessageChannel yield #13864 (pollset_poll's yield waits on a MessageChannel task, not setTimeout's clamped 4 ms; as of 2026-10-26) and the page's monitors #13865 (the page splits the one canvas into a monitor per screen for the display layout; as of 2026-10-26). 1 commit of an open pull request for every client: the physical monitor size in millimetres #13805 (SDL3 sent pixels, so a 2880-pixel window was a 2.88 m monitor; now 0, "not given"; as of 2026-10-21) | the native clients' smoke and xrdp login tests, the web login test; before the pick: Linux and Windows clients built, xrdp logins on Fedora 45 (19/19) and Debian 13 (12/12), browser logins with Asyncify and JSPI (5/5 each); each pull request's own CI upstream | FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13733 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13864 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13865 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13805
change freerdp_host     | FreeRDP master @ 472f1901f (2026-10-30) | our release-20261030.1, picked from integration-shadow-win: the Windows shadow server's two build fixes, DXGI capture that follows the secure desktop, freerdp-shadow-service with Ctrl+Alt+Del, a Unix-socket listener on Windows | `test/windows-host.ps1` (Windows Server 2025 runner) | FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13931 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13932 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13933 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13934 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13935
change sdl3_wasm        | SDL `release-3.4.18` | 1 commit: the Emscripten timers are safe to use from any thread. Since 4d8f84f161 (in 3.2.30 and 3.4) they run with pthreads too, but a timeout belongs to the thread that set it: a timer removed from another thread fired through a freed entry ("table index is out of bounds" in `SDL_Emscripten_TimerHelper`), in about 1 of 3 first sessions. 3.4.18 already has upstream's `FS.mkdir("/tmp/filedrop")` guard, which 3.2.30 needed backported (a second window, FreeRDP's retry dialog, threw `EEXIST` and hung a JSPI client after a network drop) | freerdp-web's whole suite on Asyncify and JSPI builds, 28 of 28 runs, `test-capture` and `test-reconnect` included, with the page's pointer-event fix (SDL 3.4 reads the mouse from pointer events); `SDL_timer.c` compiles with `-Werror` | libsdl-org/SDL#16587
change freerdp_tk       | its release {version} | our own connection window (Tkinter), shipped with the clients and their Python; `freerdp-tk` / `freerdp-tk.cmd` starts it. Since 0.3.0 it keeps passwords in the system's own store (Credential Manager, Keychain, Secret Service or KWallet) through keyring: the kit bundles keyring and what it needs on each OS, at the versions and SHA-256 of freerdp-tk's own uv.lock (`build/launcher.sh`, add_tk_deps) | the smoke test loads it with the bundled Python on every distribution; the build imports keyring and its backend's libraries with it (Linux, macOS)
change freerdp_web      | its release {version} | our own page, taken by its release tag | its unit tests and page checks (freerdp-web CI), then the web login test
change xrdp             | xrdp devel @ 5943357a (2026-10-14) | 127 commits on their way upstream: Wayland sessions (wlup: sway, GNOME, KDE), GNOME and KDE with a monitor per RDP monitor and the client's primary as their own (branches feature-wlup-mutter-multimon, feature-wlup-kwin-multimon), and a max_fps setting for them, KWin 6.8's custom modes (kde_output_management_v2 22), AV1 with 4:4:4, encoder paced by the client's frame acknowledgements, Opus sound fixes (#3922: 2 of its 3 commits); plus the JPEG quality byte compared as unsigned, so it builds on ARM64 (branch caps-jpeg-quality-unsigned) | the login test, Xorg and Wayland, on x86_64 and ARM64; the ARM64 fix also by a build with -funsigned-char, which fails without it | neutrinolabs/xrdp#3904 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3911 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3912 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3913 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3914 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3915 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3922
change librfxcodec      | xrdp's submodule | unchanged: the commit `xrdp` uses | built with xrdp
change libpainter       | xrdp's submodule | unchanged: the commit `xrdp` uses | built with xrdp
change xorgxrdp         | xorgxrdp devel | unchanged: the development commit whose module interface `xrdp` needs | the Xorg login
change x264             | x264 `stable` branch | unchanged: x264 has no releases | the xrdp login tests (H.264)
change pipewire_xrdp    | release v{version} | unchanged, pinned by its tag's commit; built for Fedora only, which does not package it | built in the Fedora xrdp jobs
change mutter           | Fedora 45's {version} | an opt-in for Fedora 45: Fedora's own source package plus our fix for a Wayland window that lands on the wrong monitor when the monitor layout moves its monitor (2 commits, patches/mutter/: the main monitor from the newest pending move after a layout change, also when the client acks an older configure; as of 2026-10-28), release 1.0kit1, so Fedora's next update replaces it | 20 of 20 runs of the All screens check on the right monitor (stock 51.0: 1 of 10 wrong; 0 of 11 vs 5 of 7 with the server on one CPU); build/build-mutter.sh installs it with Fedora's gnome-shell | GNOME/mutter#5162 GNOME/mutter!5438
